id: AEP28-ENV-069
title: GraphEngine execute must not run a node executor until envelope Admit allows and vector clocks are not Admit.
status: closed
priority: P0
track: aep28-library-components
wave: graph-admit-gate
plan: none
repo: NLA-AEP-v2.8-open-source
depends_on: none
scope: AEP-Components/graph-engine/lib/graph/engine.ts AEP-Components/graph-engine-admit-gate/crate README.md AEP-User-Experience/AEP-main-skill/SKILL.md CHANGELOG.md
notes: Closed. GraphEngine.execute requires admitGate default deny before nodeExecutor. A missing admitGate is deny. The local vector clock ticks only after allow and is not kernel Admit. policyEvaluator is not Admit. Kernel Admit is drift, age, future, sequence and digest replay. README, AEP-main-skill and GraphEngine README no longer teach Lamport vector clocks as live Admit. TypeScript dynAEP remains. GraphEngine is not a second kernel. Ticket close is coding close.
acceptance: GraphEngine with no admitGate denies nodeExecutor. GraphEngine with admitGate deny does not tick the vector clock. GraphEngine with admitGate allow may run nodeExecutor and then tick. A Rust crate under AEP-Components/graph-engine-admit-gate fails if engine.ts calls nodeExecutor without admitGate. README, AEP-main-skill and GraphEngine README do not teach Lamport vector clocks as live Admit. nla-policy-scan gate coding-completion and project-completion-bac on AEP-Components/graph-engine-admit-gate/crate before any ship prose.
bac: nla-policy-scan gate project-completion-bac /root/NLA-AEP-v2.8-open-source/AEP-Components/graph-engine-admit-gate/crate
